{"id": "EUVD-2026-75537", "enisaUuid": "12929511-d86f-3203-a79b-19a2111eebe6", "description": "A flaw was found in the admin backend of gvfs. The privileged gvfsd-admin daemon changes the ownership of newly created private D-Bus sockets by calling the link-following chown() function on a pathname inside a user-controlled directory. A local attacker can exploit this via a Time-of-Check Time-of-Use (TOCTOU) race condition and exchange the socket pathname with a symbolic link pointing to an arbitrary root-owned file (such as /etc/pam.d/su). The daemon subsequently follows the symlink and changes the ownership of the targeted root-owned file to the attacker's user ID. This allows an authenticated local attacker to modify critical system files, leading to a full local privilege escalation to root.", "datePublished": "2026-09-10T14:32:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T23:01:41", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:73998", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74370", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85939", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85941", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85942", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85944", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-88924", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2531456", "https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gvfs/-/issues/875"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-88924", "GHSA-8w8m-36rw-gg63"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "74fbeb49-faf0-3347-a8cc-5fc8e6c68b8b", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.2 Update Services for SAP Solutions", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.48.1-4.el9_2.1"}, {"id": "840e1001-53c2-3986-8efe-e67bc107f1aa", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.4 Update Services for SAP Solutions", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patc